  "id": "genappe",
  "title": "Genappe Rearguard",
  "date": "17 June 1815",
  "blurb": "Wellington is retreating north to Mont-Saint-Jean in a downpour. The Brussels road drops into the Dyle valley, crosses a single narrow bridge at Genappe and climbs a long, cramped street out of the town. Lord Uxbridge's cavalry waits on the rising ground beyond. Hurl your lancers through the defile before the storm turns the fields to mud.",
  "hint": "The Dyle cannot be waded below the town; the town bridge is the only crossing on the road, with fords upstream to the south-west and the Ways bridge far to the east. The street beyond is a trap for cavalry: clear it with infantry, then take the heights where the Life Guards wait.",
